The input list is changed by skipping one node, and the removed node is freed. Time complexity is `O(L)` and extra space is `O(1)`, where `L` is the list length.

## Intuition
Use recursion to find the reversed position of a node.
Then, if we want to delete the Nth node, we can be at the (N+1)th node (in a reversed sense), and delete the next node.
Handling edge cases is needed when we need to remove the head node.

